The issue is on line 425 (the return statement). Mypy seems to think `last_sequence_is_user` could be `list[Message] | bool` instead of just `bool`. This is strange. Let me check if there's an issue with the expression `last_sequence.messages and last_sequence.messages[-1].role == "user"`. 

Actually, `last_sequence.messages` is a `list[Message]`, so `last_sequence.messages and ...` returns either `False` (if `last_sequence.messages` is empty) or the result of the comparison. In Python, `and` returns the first falsy value or the last truthy value. So if `last_sequence.messages` is empty list (falsy), it returns `[]`, not `False`. That's the issue!

